{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Investigation on origin/main 5a6c8a19f4f (2026-11-01), in-process, no LLM runs.\n\nReproduction with pass1.material_fingerprint on a one-criterion AC section: untagged 82d01115bad8af65; ticked 82d01115bad8af65 (unchanged); tag added at the start cc312ff32fd715a4 (changed); tag plus provenance line a046e64e4feb7689. provenance_gaps: 1 gap after the tag alone, 0 after the provenance line. COMPLETION_REMEDIATION_GUIDANCE contains neither \"provenance\" nor \"review-plan\" nor any statement that the edit stales the attestation, and shows no example of where the tag goes.\n\nNo main commit since the ticket was filed touches txn.py, completion_reconcile.py, material_diff.py, det_operator_attested.py, det_measurement_provenance.py, or completion_criteria.py.\n\nPrior intent: f680-4224-6553-48ca (talkable-ungodly-whapuku) and 2f56-313f-6175-41b1 (binary-cobwebby-bittern) both recorded that the tag is reviewed plan material and must stay in the fingerprint (anti-tamper; retagging after certification is the laundering vector). 2f56's shipped mitigation was to say so in the close-precheck messages (txn.ensure_attested_items_valid already says \"this description edit stales a signed plan-review attestation\"). The verifier's remediation is the remaining surface without that statement and without the provenance-line requirement. The original AC \"adding or removing [non-codebase] leaves the attestation current\" contradicts that intent, so the description is revised to fix the remediation text instead. 2f56 left a direction-sensitive exemption (tag-remove / provenance-add exempt, tag-add material) as a possible future ticket needing a signing-contract review; it would not help this incident, which was a tag ADD.\n\nTag position: the close precheck, the completion verifier prompt (completion_verifier.md, \"tag at the start of the checkbox text\"), and ADR 0043 all recognize the tag only at the start, so they agree with each other. The gap is that nothing tells the author: 28 AC lines in 22 tickets carry the tag at the END of the line (27 already ticked; fleece-grave-noolbenger's is open), and those are silently treated as untagged. Same root as this bug on the remediation side (the guidance never says where the tag goes, fixed here); the silent non-recognition is filed separately."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793522800870129001,"uuid":"89d36e4c-c992-4666-9c68-f63c4f70ec04"}